<GuideLayout
  title="China vs Vietnam Activewear Manufacturing: A Sourcing Comparison for Brands"
  type="Comparison Center"
  description="Compare China and Vietnam activewear manufacturing by supplier depth, fabric access, MOQ, customization, lead time, compliance and buyer fit."
>
  <p>China and Vietnam are both important apparel sourcing markets, but they are not interchangeable. For activewear brands, the best choice depends on product complexity, fabric sourcing, MOQ needs, customization level and the kind of supplier support required.</p>

  <h2>Quick Answer</h2>
  <p>China is often stronger for flexible private label activewear, fabric variety, low-to-mid MOQ testing and fast supplier coordination. Vietnam can be a good fit for larger-volume, stable programs when the buyer has mature planning and clear compliance requirements.</p>

  <h2>Comparison Table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Factor</th><th>China</th><th>Vietnam</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Fabric access</td><td>Broad access to nylon, polyester, seamless, recycled and specialty performance fabrics</td><td>Strong for selected programs but often less flexible for small testing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>MOQ flexibility</td><td>Often better for small brand launches and private label testing</td><td>Usually better for larger, planned volume</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customization</td><td>Strong logo, label, packaging, pattern and ODM support</td><td>Strong when specs are fixed and production is repeatable</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Lead time</td><td>Fast when fabric and trims are locally available</td><td>Efficient for stable programs with clear planning</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When China Is a Better Fit</h2>
  <p>China is often practical for activewear startups, online fitness brands and buyers who need fast sample iteration, multiple product categories, fabric choices and private label flexibility. This is especially useful for leggings, sports bras, yoga sets, gym tops and athleisure capsules.</p>

  <h2>When Vietnam Is a Better Fit</h2>
  <p>Vietnam can work well for larger buyers with stable forecasts, clear tech packs, repeatable styles and established compliance requirements. It is less ideal when the brand needs many small tests across different fabrics, colors and logo methods.</p>

